          "description": "Ions per formula unit of each electrolyte, in the ion order H+, NH4+, Na+, Ca++, HSO4-, SO4--, NO3-, Cl-, MSA- (the chemical formulas; e.g. letovicite (NH4)3H(SO4)2 = 3 NH4+ + HSO4- + SO4--). CaCO3 carries only its Ca++ (MOSAIC has no carbonate ion); only conform_electrolytes.esm reads its row (electrolytes_to_ions puts CaCO3 in calcium and sets carbonate from it separately). An activity is gamma^nu times the product of the ion molalities raised to these counts, nu being the row sum."
        },
